hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17942","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Marzuq, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah, from Ziyad ibn Nuaym al-Hadrami, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Four things Allah has ordained in Islam; whoever brings three will avail him nothing until he brings them all: prayer, alms, fasting Ramadan, and Hajj to the House."
